WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.385
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:09.129
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:15.216
Unit two: Learning Styles. Today you will use gerunds as subjects to talk about studying.

4
00:00:15.516 --> 00:00:18.331
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:23.196
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.202
Visual learner.

7
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:29.191
Visual learner means a person who learns best by seeing.

8
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:32.410
As a visual learner, I love diagrams.

9
00:00:33.017 --> 00:00:35.472
Your turn. Say: Visual learner.

10
00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:39.451
Visual learner.

11
00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:41.473
Auditory learner.

12
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:45.714
Auditory learner means a person who learns best by listening.

13
00:00:46.317 --> 00:00:48.734
Auditory learners enjoy podcasts.

14
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.258
Your turn. Say: Auditory learner.

15
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.519
Auditory learner.

16
00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:58.447
Kinesthetic.

17
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.972
Kinesthetic means learning by doing and moving.

18
00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:04.885
Kinesthetic learners like experiments.

19
00:01:05.483 --> 00:01:08.356
Your turn. Say: Kinesthetic.

20
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.259
Kinesthetic.

21
00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:14.459
Retain information.

22
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.703
Retain information means to keep facts in your memory.

23
00:01:19.317 --> 00:01:22.036
Colour notes help me retain information.

24
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.964
Your turn. Say: Retain information.

25
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.335
Retain information.

26
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:32.270
Study technique.

27
00:01:33.283 --> 00:01:35.782
Study technique means a method for studying.

28
00:01:36.383 --> 00:01:38.789
Flashcards are my best study technique.

29
00:01:39.383 --> 00:01:42.279
Your turn. Say: Study technique.

30
00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:46.297
Study technique.

31
00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.214
Concentration.

32
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:52.273
Concentration means the ability to think about one thing.

33
00:01:52.883 --> 00:01:54.918
Music breaks my concentration.

34
00:01:55.517 --> 00:01:58.691
Your turn. Say: Concentration.

35
00:02:01.533 --> 00:02:02.894
Concentration.

36
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:04.790
Memorize.

37
00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:09.223
Memorize means to learn something so you remember it exactly.

38
00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:12.327
I memorize ten new words every day.

39
00:02:12.917 --> 00:02:15.906
Your turn. Say: Memorize.

40
00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:19.942
Memorize.

41
00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:21.731
Comprehension.

42
00:02:22.717 --> 00:02:25.633
Comprehension means understanding what you read or hear.

43
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.668
Reading every day improves comprehension.

44
00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:32.423
Your turn. Say: Comprehension.

45
00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:36.303
Comprehension.

46
00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.121
Note-taking.

47
00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:41.894
Note-taking means writing short notes while you learn.

48
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:44.599
Good note-taking saves time later.

49
00:02:45.183 --> 00:02:48.010
Your turn. Say: Note-taking.

50
00:02:50.867 --> 00:02:52.251
Note-taking.

51
00:02:53.017 --> 00:02:53.913
Review.

52
00:02:54.917 --> 00:02:57.230
Review means studying something again.

53
00:02:57.817 --> 00:03:00.083
A quick review helps before the exam.

54
00:03:00.683 --> 00:03:03.324
Your turn. Say: Review.

55
00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.063
Review.

56
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:09.120
Practice test.

57
00:03:10.117 --> 00:03:12.871
Practice test means a test you do to prepare.

58
00:03:13.483 --> 00:03:15.692
I took three practice tests this week.

59
00:03:16.283 --> 00:03:18.866
Your turn. Say: Practice test.

60
00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.003
Practice test.

61
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.716
Feedback.

62
00:03:25.717 --> 00:03:28.413
Feedback means comments about how well you did.

63
00:03:29.017 --> 00:03:31.028
My teacher's feedback was helpful.

64
00:03:31.617 --> 00:03:34.234
Your turn. Say: Feedback.

65
00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:37.973
Feedback.

66
00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:42.464
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:45.270
Visal, how do you learn best?

68
00:03:46.383 --> 00:03:51.555
I'm a visual learner. Drawing diagrams helps me retain information.

69
00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.580
What study technique do you use?

70
00:03:55.683 --> 00:03:59.262
Reviewing my notes every night is my main technique.

71
00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:02.257
And before an exam?

72
00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:08.322
Taking practice tests builds my confidence, and feedback shows my mistakes.

73
00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:10.862
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.529
Grammar focus: Gerunds as subjects.

75
00:04:14.829 --> 00:04:16.097
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:16.783 --> 00:04:18.597
Reviewing notes helps memory.

77
00:04:19.483 --> 00:04:22.203
Taking practice tests builds confidence.

78
00:04:23.117 --> 00:04:24.896
Drawing diagrams is useful.

79
00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:29.818
A gerund subject is singular, so use 'helps', 'builds' or 'is'.

80
00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:34.431
Be careful! Don't say: Review notes helps memory.

81
00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:39.121
Say: Reviewing notes helps memory.

82
00:04:39.421 --> 00:04:41.804
Use the -ing form when a verb is the subject.

83
00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.055
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:45.867 --> 00:04:47.251
How I Learn Best.

85
00:04:47.551 --> 00:04:52.151
Some students are visual learners, some are auditory, and some are kinesthetic.

86
00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:57.221
As a visual learner, I retain information better with diagrams.

87
00:04:58.233 --> 00:05:01.800
My study technique includes note-taking and regular review.

88
00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:06.320
Taking a practice test before an exam improves my comprehension.

89
00:05:07.333 --> 00:05:10.099
Getting feedback from my teacher helps me improve.

90
00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.144
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:15.983 --> 00:05:17.658
blank notes helps memory.

92
00:05:17.958 --> 00:05:22.052
A, Reviewing. B, Review. C, Reviews.

93
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.785
The answer is A: Reviewing.

94
00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:32.412
A person who learns best by listening is an blank learner.

95
00:05:32.712 --> 00:05:36.377
A, auditory. B, visual. C, kinesthetic.

96
00:05:39.933 --> 00:05:41.991
The answer is A: auditory.

97
00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.405
Comments about how well you did are blank.

98
00:05:45.705 --> 00:05:50.125
A, feedback. B, a review. C, concentration.

99
00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:55.910
The answer is A: feedback.

100
00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.170
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:01.017 --> 00:06:03.121
What study technique works best for you?

102
00:06:11.917 --> 00:06:13.336
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:13.636 --> 00:06:20.642
Making flashcards works best for me. Testing myself with flashcards helps me memorize new words quickly.

104
00:06:20.942 --> 00:06:22.686
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:27.966
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and gerunds as subjects.

106
00:06:28.266 --> 00:06:32.416
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

107
00:06:32.716 --> 00:06:35.205
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

108
00:06:35.505 --> 00:06:39.179
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

